diff --git a/FAQ.md b/FAQ.md
index 84d01f2..41b4128 100644
--- a/FAQ.md
+++ b/FAQ.md
@@ -121,6 +121,19 @@ $ mkdir -p "$dir"
 $ rg --generate complete-zsh > "$dir/_rg"
 ```
 
+Alternatively, if you don't want to bother saving the completion script to a
+file, you can dynamically generate and source it in your `.zshrc`:
+
+```
+source <(rg --generate complete-zsh)
+```
+
+Beware that this approach is slower since it regenerates the completion
+script every time a new shell starts. (In the ballpark of ~4 milliseconds as
+of the time of writing this.) That's probably not even enough to notice on
+its own, but it can add up if you do this for multiple tools and find
+yourself opening shells frequently.
+
 For **PowerShell**, create the completions:
 
 ```
diff --git a/ci/test-complete b/ci/test-complete
index 3793aff..1d93f01 100755
--- a/ci/test-complete
+++ b/ci/test-complete
@@ -13,7 +13,11 @@ get_comp_args() {
     # Our completion function recognises a special variable which tells it to
     # dump the _arguments specs and then just return. But do this in a sub-shell
     # anyway to avoid any weirdness
-    ( _RG_COMPLETE_LIST_ARGS=1 source $1 )
+    #
+    # Note that sourcing the file only defines `_rg` (it no longer calls it
+    # automatically unless it detects that it's being autoloaded as part of
+    # a real completion), so we call it explicitly here ourselves.
+    ( _RG_COMPLETE_LIST_ARGS=1 source $1; _rg )
 }
 
